{"schema": "document.v2", "source_id": "eur-lex.europa.eu", "source_name": "EUR-Lex", "url": "https://european-union.europa.eu/index_en", "canonical_url": "https://european-union.europa.eu/index_en", "fetch_time": "2026-06-01T15:51:33.582706+00:00", "language": "en", "title": "Your gateway to the European Union", "published_date": "2026-01-06T12:00:00+00:00", "updated_date": null, "doc_type": "Blog/News", "programme": ["Other/NA"], "finance_instrument": [], "stage": null, "actors": [], "tech_area": [], "monetary_values": [], "summary_150w": "All featured news are available in the 24 EU official languages via machine translation. The European Commission will start implementing a new plan to phase out animal testing for chemical safety assessments. It lays out steps towards moving to innovative non-animal approaches and preserves safety evaluations. The plan strengthens the existing EU chemicals legislation, REACH. The jury of the European Union Prize for Literature announced the 2026 winners. Dora Kaprálová, from Czechia won the Grand Prix with \"Mariborská hypnóza\" (Maribor Hypnosis), while special mentions went to Hélène Frédérick from France and Vladimir Vujović from Montenegro. The European Heritage Awards have announced 30 winners. Among the five Grand Prix winners there figure the Cypriot Fiddler research project that documents the life stories of Greek Cypriot and Turkish Cypriot musicians and Din l-Art Ħelwa that has protected Malta’s historic sites since 1965. Follow Sven, Elena and Sofia as they embark on an exciting trip across Europe. Follow Marie on her picnic to discover why food in the EU is both tasty and safe\nDiscover the EU’s priorities for 2024-2029, promoting a free and democratic Europe, developing a strong and secure Europe, establishing a prosperous and competitive Europe. Find out how many EU Member States there are, how big the EU economy is, how people live in the EU, and other useful facts about the EU. Discover what the EU does for citizens, how it protects rights, promotes prosperity and strives to make the world a safer place. Teaching material, games and much more about the European Union and its activities, for children, teenagers, teachers and parents. Share this page\n\nReferences\n• Source — 06 Jan 2026 — https://european-union.europa.eu/index_en", "key_points": [], "implications": {"innovation_direction": [], "capital_structure": [], "regulatory_change": []}, "links": {"pdf": [], "dataset": [], "related": []}, "celex_id": null, "call_id": null, "award_id": null, "tags": [], "dedupe_signature": "0b87c8e792e2414e0ff251020f44ada2bbffeccd86c1f8fcbe31bd644c7532f8", "embeddings": null, "extraction_notes": null}
